# No temporary leftovers

After any modification or diagnostic work in DMS:

- Delete temporary probe/debug scripts (e.g. `_tmp_*.php`, `tmp_*.php`, `*probe*.php` created for inspection).
- Remove throwaway inline debug code (`var_dump`, `print_r`, `dd`, temporary `echo` diagnostics) before finishing.
- Do not leave unused temporary pages in the project root or elsewhere.
- Prefer one-off Shell/`php -r` checks over committing temporary PHP files when possible.
- If a temporary file was created during the session, delete it before ending the task unless the user explicitly asks to keep it.
